# Documentation Authority Map

> Review date: {{DATE}}.

This document defines which project documents own which topics, to prevent duplicated rules, stale parallel summaries, and unnecessary context loading.

## Principle

Write each rule once in its owner document. Other documents link to the owner or carry only a thin audience-specific summary.

## Doc Trees

| Tree | Path | Audience |
|---|---|---|
| Requirements | [requirements/](../requirements/) | Implementation and validation source |
| Technical | [technical/](.) | Implementation/configuration/operations details |
| ADRs | [adr/](../adr/) | Consequential decisions and rationale |
| Decisions | [../../decisions/](../../decisions/) | Lighter-weight dated decisions |
| Archive | [archive/](../archive/) | Historical only |

## Authority By Topic

| Topic | Authority |
|---|---|
| Project overview | [requirements/00-overview.md](../requirements/00-overview.md) |
| Requirements index and identifiers | [requirements/README.md](../requirements/README.md) |
| Requirement changes | [requirements/CHANGELOG.md](../requirements/CHANGELOG.md) |
| Open discovery/validation questions | [requirements/04-open-questions.md](../requirements/04-open-questions.md) |
| Pending decisions needing approval | [../../OPEN_DECISIONS.md](../../OPEN_DECISIONS.md) |
| Consequential architecture/process decisions | [adr/](../adr/) |
| Lightweight dated decisions | [../../decisions/](../../decisions/) |
| Documentation conventions and Markdown headers | [01-documentation-conventions.md](01-documentation-conventions.md) |
| Current implementation inventory | [05-implementation-index.md](05-implementation-index.md) |
| Software release history | [../../CHANGELOG.md](../../CHANGELOG.md) |

## Reading Orders

### General Project Work

1. `CURRENT_CONTEXT.md`
2. [requirements/00-overview.md](../requirements/00-overview.md)
3. Relevant requirements, technical, or ADR documents

### Implementation Status Or Code Navigation

1. `CURRENT_CONTEXT.md`, when not already loaded
2. [technical/README.md](README.md)
3. [05-implementation-index.md](05-implementation-index.md)
4. Relevant owner documents named by the implementation index
5. Named code locations and targeted searches

### Requirements Work

1. [requirements/README.md](../requirements/README.md)
2. Relevant requirement documents
3. [requirements/CHANGELOG.md](../requirements/CHANGELOG.md) when requirements change

## Changelog Discipline

| Change type | Update |
|---|---|
| Requirement or acceptance criterion | [requirements/CHANGELOG.md](../requirements/CHANGELOG.md) |
| Important implementation or process decision | [../../decisions/](../../decisions/) or an ADR |
| Documentation ownership or reading order | This file |
| Current implementation state, code locations, validation commands | [05-implementation-index.md](05-implementation-index.md) |
| Software release | [../../CHANGELOG.md](../../CHANGELOG.md) |

## Post-Implementation Doc Hygiene

After meaningful implementation, configuration, or documentation work, ask: does any referenced document describe intent rather than reality? If yes, update the owner document before closing the task.

## Archive Rule

Do not load [archive/](../archive/) for active work unless historical context is explicitly needed.
